  "text": "Hibernia is a Celtic land. Hibernia is an ancient name. The name means winter country. Greek and Roman writers used the name for both Ireland and, occasionally, Britain. To Mediterranean peoples the rainy chill of Ireland appeared to be a perpetual winter. The name therefore came from the perceived weather of the island.",
